node_modules/
dist/
.orchestrator/
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
coverage/

# `.cao-files/` is local working material for running cao on itself (workflows, task scopes,
# baseline captures). It is never committed: cao writes completion markers into the workflow
# YAML mid-run and tasks commit their own work, so a tracked copy dirties the tree and breaks
# the run. Run state never lands there either — that is `.orchestrator/`, ignored above.
.cao-files/

# `.agents/` (the cao skills for Claude Code and Codex) and `scripts/install-cao-skills.ps1`
# (the installer that copies them into a user's agent directories) are tracked as well. They
# are the supported way to get the skills, so they are source, not local scratch. Do not add
# an ignore rule for them: `.gitignore` does not apply to files already tracked, so the rule
# would do nothing except silently swallow new skill files added under `.agents/`.

# Local Claude Code instructions for this checkout; not project source.
CLAUDE.md
